From: OpenAI Codex <codex@openai.com>
Subject: [PATCH] clk: en7523: initialize the reset update value

The reset update value is a local variable. Combining a reset bit with
its uninitialized contents is undefined behavior and can leave the bit
set when deasserting a normal reset or asserting an inverted PCIe reset.
Assign the complete masked value for each bank polarity before the
regmap update so reset consumers get the requested level.

Signed-off-by: OpenAI Codex <codex@openai.com>
---

--- a/drivers/clk/clk-en7523.c
+++ b/drivers/clk/clk-en7523.c
@@ -1034,9 +1034,9 @@
 
 	/* For PCIC reset logic is inverted, 0:assert 1:deassert*/
 	if (addr == REG_NP_SCU_PCIC)
-		val |= assert ? 0 : BIT(id % RST_NR_PER_BANK);
+		val = assert ? 0 : BIT(id % RST_NR_PER_BANK);
 	else
-		val |= assert ? BIT(id % RST_NR_PER_BANK) : 0;
+		val = assert ? BIT(id % RST_NR_PER_BANK) : 0;
 
 	return regmap_update_bits(rst_data->map, addr,
 				  BIT(id % RST_NR_PER_BANK), val);
